     - Slugs contain only alphanumeric and hyphens
     - Lowercase slugs
     - Default "index" for empty results

3. **Schema & Edge Cases:**
   - **Current Behavior:**
     ```rust
     url_to_slug("https://example.com/") → ""  // EMPTY!
     url_to_slug("https://example.com///") → ""  // EMPTY!
     url_to_slug("https://example.com/???") → ""  // All filtered!
     ```
   - **Expected Behavior:**
     ```rust
     url_to_slug("https://example.com/") → "index"
     url_to_slug("https://example.com///") → "index"
     url_to_slug("https://example.com/???") → "index"
     url_to_slug("https://example.com/docs/") → "docs"
     ```
   - **Edge Cases:**
     - URL "/" → "index"
     - URL with only special chars → "index"
     - URL with unicode → filter to alphanumeric + keep ASCII
     - Very long slug (>255 chars) → truncate?

IMPLEMENTATION:

```rust
fn url_to_slug(url: &str) -> String {
    let path = url::Url::parse(url)
        .map(|u| u.path().to_string())
        .unwrap_or_else(|_| url.to_string());

    let slug = path
        .trim_matches('/')
        .replace(['/', '.'], "-")
        .chars()
        .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-')
        .collect::<String>()
        .to_lowercase();

    // NEW: Ensure non-empty slug
    if slug.is_empty() {
        "index".to_string()
    } else {
        slug
    }
}
```

